    "body": "## Motivation\n\nP2P senders need the receiver's actual parameter dtype before writing directly into its memory. The current address and size metadata cannot distinguish BF16 from FP16: both use two bytes per element, but interpret those bytes differently.\n\nBuilt on #42820. **Companion PR: [radixark/miles#4016](https://github.com/radixark/miles/pull/4016) — validate receiver dtypes before P2P weight transfers.** The companion extends radixark/miles#3969 and rejects incompatible transfers using this metadata. This SGLang change publishes the information; it does not itself enforce the check.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Publish `weight_dtypes` from the registered model's named parameters, using names such as `bfloat16`.\n- Store and return the mapping with the existing `(role, tp_rank)` metadata, preserving separate target and draft records.\n- Keep the existing `remote_instance_transfer_engine_info` tuple unchanged. Publishers without dtype metadata return an empty mapping, and consumers that read only the original field continue working.\n- Extend the role-publication unit test to check the dtype mappings and preservation of the existing response.\n\nDeploy this change before the stricter companion Miles sender, or deploy both together.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nTested the paired changes in a fork on **`Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct`**, with two runs per case below. Each used two H100 nodes, one trainer GPU and one inference GPU. All six runs completed 11 training steps with initial weight equality, successful EFA transfers and finite nonzero gradients.\n\nThese are short execution checks with synthetic rewards, not convergence or reconnect tests. Every run logged an existing forced-termination warning during inference shutdown.\n\nThe repository-pinned pre-commit hooks passed locally on all 3 PR files without modifying them, and the upstream [full-repository lint job](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38160111003/job/114531049147) passed. The extended runtime unit test has not been rerun on this upstream port; the fork benchmark results do not validate this exact tree.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n| Case | First weight sync | Warm-sync median | Registered memory per sender |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Previous P2P, with sender dtype corrected | 13.73–13.95 s | 0.275–0.276 s | 0.92 GiB |\n| Loader-based P2P, without this guard | 10.47–10.55 s | 0.280–0.282 s | 1.00 GiB |\n| Loader-based P2P + dtype guard | 10.62–10.77 s | 0.269–0.275 s | 1.00 GiB |\n\nRanges show the two runs; each warm median covers ten syncs. Timings include the whole weight-sync operation and GPU completion. Runs used different node pairs in parallel, so small differences should not be treated as speedups. Memory counts application buffer registrations, not total process memory; the loader-based implementation uses two 512 MiB buffers.\n\nThe companion Miles guard checked **170 BF16 tensor layouts once per connection**. Local metadata validation averaged **94 µs with the guard versus 51 µs without**, an observed difference of approximately **43 µs per connection**, not per training step. Publisher serialization and HTTP metadata overhead were not isolated, and no speed benchmark was run on this upstream port.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).",
